# =============================================================================
# ending.dialogue — THE ENDING.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ella stays off-screen — heard, never shown. The weight lands on sound and on
# what we don't see.
#   ~ ending  played when the ending scene loads.
# =============================================================================

~ ending
The cat carries a strand of silk out into the dawn garden. The once-unreachable golden window is now a warm open door, at ground level at last. We see the cat from behind, small, facing the light.
Ella: Oh... Hey. It's you. You came back. You always come back, and then you—
The cat does not run. He steps inside.
Ella: ...Tobers.
This time he doesn't bolt. The screen holds on the open door, the warm light, the dawn. A chair creaks, a girl settles, a quiet "there you are." And then — for the first time — purring.
The camera drifts up to the rafters, where a single long leg rests in the shadow, and eight small points of light watch, content. The little spiders gather around the Weaver.
Little Spider: Did he do it, Grandfather? Did he stay?
Weaver: He stayed. The last thread is spun.
Weaver: Come. We have a great deal of weeping in the rain ahead of us — there are always more frightened little embers in the world who've forgotten they're allowed.
=> END
